eligibility:
• The woman must be an SHG member, mainly from weaker sections.
• She must live in a covered district. Running in Ayodhya, Gorakhpur, Varanasi, Kaushambi and Jhansi;
Lucknow, Prayagraj, Mirzapur and others are to follow.

how_to_apply:
There is no open public application. Eligible households are taken from the SECC 2011 / Awaas+ lists and
verified by the Gram Sabha. Contact the Gram Panchayat / Block office to check if your name is on the list;
registration is done by the block official on pmayg.nic.in (Awaas+ 2024 app uses face authentication).

benefit:
Take-home ration with 600 kcal, 18-20 g protein and micronutrients for 300 days a year; iron-folic acid tablets;
health check-up and referral; nutrition and health education; menstrual hygiene promotion; peer educator
programme; and skill/livelihood training.

eligibility:
• Depends on the component: any woman in distress for OSC/181; working women for Sakhi Niwas;
pregnant/lactating women for PMMVY; working mothers for Palna; destitute, trafficked or distressed
women for Shakti Sadan.
